#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100607 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable"}] :question/id #uuid "66ec04a0-2af8-5187-98b2-b06eedd5b0a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4406" :question/problem "Find $CD$, if \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/1a753977affc5cc3dda18c9206116e1132254bccebd1e3f2545bea75bcc38f18.png)\nand \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/b99016bca94adc5de11eddef950fa13fc4349aaf95387468d07f294c409d029d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/64b831a66cdd9a3176d1eb916dfae189b41eb1f0f3ed3184797f92e404957878.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100608 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71ff07eb-2e16-529e-b17c-1bf7cb9703bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Entry of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "3a696ed3-e341-5ea6-bf17-681ba8e386c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4407" :question/problem "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/c6c7e580cfd96bc23c55742535ceb40a94635c2a44b911e0d08311c3a599c2fa.png)" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $A$ by the $2$nd column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100655 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "c3ed8d05-758d-5ae0-bf57-3779fde6020b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5885" :question/problem "Compute the product \n $\\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n \t\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} {\\color{green}\\checkmark} {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} = \n\t\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t&= \n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        (-1)\\cdot 2 & (-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\n        0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot (-5)\\\n        (-2)\\cdot 2 & (-2)\\cdot (-5)\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \\[5pt]\n\n\t&=\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -2 & 5 \\\n       0 &  0 \\\n       -4 &  10 \n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11187f3b-1bcb-596c-9f51-5d9418a82bfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320596} {:answer/id #uuid "392edab7-655c-5162-a4b4-bada8ec33f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320597} {:answer/id #uuid "460f3c33-9362-55a2-af9e-ab4d0693fcc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 24 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320598} {:answer/id #uuid "61330e29-da40-50af-9e64-86a4db773926" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320599} {:answer/id #uuid "eb60d008-dcf2-50be-a70e-3a28969daef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & -24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11187f3b-1bcb-596c-9f51-5d9418a82bfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320596} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3da0ad9-f9c5-5cd8-a0a9-221064800de5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07a1dff2-e7c5-5216-8b23-f0d5e4981e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-1035" :question/problem "Find $ST$,  if  $S=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ matrix and $T$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $T,$ so $S$ and $T$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{T}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={ST}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $ST,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,24=2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$ST=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d58ece9-34ea-5b33-aa5f-f1c6e5a54363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320603} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a2c60d-090f-500a-81f8-414c839480e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -50 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320604} {:answer/id #uuid "07206503-9bdf-520d-8f1b-af27d99bc151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -30 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320605} {:answer/id #uuid "34e44aa3-757c-5283-b65b-c81a20ecd048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320606} {:answer/id #uuid "35ac52c1-8144-53ad-ada0-f42f9a99cd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d58ece9-34ea-5b33-aa5f-f1c6e5a54363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320603} :answer-field/id #uuid "306d5f73-1c33-5e04-bb7d-2e3d15364236" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26f62605-f12e-5958-a440-a6004880b9ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-1038" :question/problem "$[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}]=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10\\cdot 1 & -10\\cdot (-5) & -10\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 6\\cdot 1 & 6\\cdot (-5) & 6\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 8\\cdot 1 & 8\\cdot (-5) & 8\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283267 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "252f0c75-7179-57a2-9665-70b5ebb8d710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 10 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283269} {:answer/id #uuid "3da91b23-c9b6-5724-bae6-01fcb033562a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283270} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5f6ce3-4413-5f1d-a3ff-afcaf4a9ab5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 10 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283271} {:answer/id #uuid "27016ec8-5211-58f4-88fa-593840b3ca68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283272} {:answer/id #uuid "cba1ecc5-4c67-581a-ab81-8986c6b7d25e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27016ec8-5211-58f4-88fa-593840b3ca68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283272} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5836791-ef34-5548-8772-a696bcf23ef4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc62761a-709a-52d5-ab50-f0dbc3395108" :question/math-academy-id "q-129495" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-15=2\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,3=2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-9=1\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 6+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,10=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b880d45c-201a-5580-98af-87ee30ea651d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320610} {:answer/id #uuid "9645efe6-75ef-565e-9866-844ac5d4107c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320611} {:answer/id #uuid "f050807e-f61b-5057-b7c3-7ed60912f070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320612} {:answer/id #uuid "9f229e6c-2aeb-507d-8b93-6853b7fa7032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320613} {:answer/id #uuid "d40096ae-a894-5da9-81ca-25494ccfc531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f050807e-f61b-5057-b7c3-7ed60912f070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320612} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd8ae80c-92ec-598e-bc37-4f1a3c90a0cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19539af7-afd1-5493-a91f-368214eb0f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-129496" :question/problem "Find $XY$,  if  $X=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $Y=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $X$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $Y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $X$ and $3$ rows in $Y,$ so $X$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={XY}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $XY,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}22 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,22=5\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,9=5\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$XY=[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71ff07eb-2e16-529e-b17c-1bf7cb9703bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Entry of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b168663-4ff1-5cb7-a523-72e37c5bea60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320617} {:answer/id #uuid "03d1d358-9205-5c89-bf3e-f94d0db09915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320618} {:answer/id #uuid "78c61d0f-dab8-5a68-ada9-3c93024283d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320619} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d772d2-e6c8-53fb-a8e3-596764f53508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320620} {:answer/id #uuid "4f923ae1-efbd-521b-896e-a8674c72db2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03d1d358-9205-5c89-bf3e-f94d0db09915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320618} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a8802b-891e-5913-9d0e-b5efb6e432e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fdcfbdca-910c-5788-bb4a-31896ba32ff6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130111" :question/problem "Let $S=UV.$ What is the value of ${s}_{13}$, if\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $1$st row in $U$ by the $3$rd column in $V$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{13} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-6-6+5 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b384850-051d-5f19-bd06-c25a7d4f69a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 16 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320624} {:answer/id #uuid "47f2c1e2-7813-52a6-af9e-3f0d8f48a315" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320625} {:answer/id #uuid "036c69e8-cee0-5207-aa3c-688f2ff9474e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320626} {:answer/id #uuid "de8502e2-d4a1-5fde-aac3-8a8ec5ece106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320627} {:answer/id #uuid "4e34b7a2-3956-5c99-9d60-e80995b41e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "036c69e8-cee0-5207-aa3c-688f2ff9474e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320626} :answer-field/id #uuid "89c449d2-b031-57e3-9a23-e91e2d7b076a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5783d1a2-5e53-530f-912a-eb9c163daa2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130136" :question/problem "$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 1 & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 4 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d1b563-c442-5f45-b5b2-cced9f2ef7d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283297} {:answer/id #uuid "85be6d02-8a04-550c-aaac-073d769a8386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283298} {:answer/id #uuid "61c02b9a-f5e1-56ec-afca-fb80e109623b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283299} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d91f57-91a5-5213-9b84-4dafcb90ae3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283300} {:answer/id #uuid "1a888825-78b2-540d-982a-9c24c232a0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d1b563-c442-5f45-b5b2-cced9f2ef7d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283297} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bec1557-23b0-5d91-b1d1-736d872c20bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dc1caab-e8b2-5f4c-af54-cbacb852a075" :question/math-academy-id "q-13635" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 1 & (-3)\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac2d41b9-a4e0-5932-86c4-15e0dad75b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac2d41b9-a4e0-5932-86c4-15e0dad75b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320631} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a93e15-0e84-5909-858e-fec0bdb52b9e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320630} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b614554d-78c7-5719-84f0-2ac8323e9ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b614554d-78c7-5719-84f0-2ac8323e9ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320633} :answer-field/id #uuid "8896f6db-7a76-5b65-aada-105e4764b093" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320632} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc8a61d-1f90-5e4e-b095-be6